  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <h3>Are my photos uploaded to a server?</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>No.</strong> The KodiniTools Collage Maker processes all images exclusively locally in your browser. Your photos never leave your device and are never transferred to our servers. Fully GDPR compliant.
  </p>

  <h3>Can I also have the collage printed?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes — export the collage at high resolution (at least 2480×3508px for A4 at 300 DPI) and send the file to an online print service like Shutterfly, Snapfish or Vistaprint.
  </p>

  <h3>Which input formats are supported?</h3>
  <p>
    JPG, PNG and WebP — all common smartphone and camera formats are compatible.
  </p>

  <h3>How many images can I use in one collage?</h3>
  <p>
    Up to 9 images per collage depending on the layout. For larger mosaics, choose a layout with more slots.
  </p>

  <div class="tip-box">
    <p><strong>Design tip:</strong> A <strong>white gutter</strong> (2–5px) between images looks clean and modern. A <strong>black background without gutter</strong> looks dramatic and is ideal for high-contrast photos. For Instagram grids, a consistent color tone across all images works best.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Photo Collage as a Gift: Tips for Printing</h2>

  <p>
    For photo printing, we recommend these settings:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li>Set resolution to <strong>at least 300 DPI</strong> (corresponds to 2480×3508px for A4)</li>
    <li>Export as <strong>JPG at 95–100% quality</strong></li>
    <li>Confirm the print format (A4, A3, square) with the print service</li>
    <li>Request a proof PDF before ordering</li>
  </ol>

